  "description": "NETVUG crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C122 H108 Gd4 N12 O22,2.5(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd7 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd8 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.454-3.803 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 93.79-112.26°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd4(μ3-OH)2L6(acac)4]·2.5CH3CN. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
